The `findOrCreateMany` method crashes when `onConflictDoNothing()` skips inserts due to concurrent writers, because skipped categories aren't in either `insertedRecords` or `existingCategories`, causing `categoryMap.get(name)!` to return `undefined`.

## Changes

- **Re-fetch after insert**: Query all requested categories after the insert operation to capture any created by concurrent writers
- **Remove unsafe assertion**: Replace `categoryMap.get(name)!` with explicit validation that throws descriptive errors on missing categories
- **Optimize result building**: Use for-loop instead of map/filter to avoid intermediate arrays with undefined values

## Before

```typescript
const insertedRecords = await this.db
  .insert(categories)
  .values(insertRecords)
  .onConflictDoNothing()
  .returning();

newCategories = CategoryMapper.toDomainList(insertedRecords);
const allCategories = [...existingCategories, ...newCategories];
const categoryMap = new Map(allCategories.map((c) => [c.name, c]));

return normalizedNames.map((name) => categoryMap.get(name)!); // ❌ crashes if concurrent insert
```

## After

```typescript
await this.db
  .insert(categories)
  .values(insertRecords)
  .onConflictDoNothing()
  .returning();

// Re-fetch to handle race conditions
const allCategories = await this.findByNames(normalizedNames);
const categoryMap = new Map(allCategories.map((c) => [c.name, c]));

const result: Category[] = [];
for (const name of normalizedNames) {
  const category = categoryMap.get(name);
  if (!category) {
    throw new Error(`Failed to find or create the requested categories: ...`);
  }
  result.push(category);
}
return result; // ✅ safe with validation
```

